		{
			"id": 1947350,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/115374177252675510",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman :11ty:",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/14ce4eedb6fa8c93ac6e7e3bb2fe381ed3e096f00f61e664def82c368d89c1d7.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-14T19:30:33.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@webreflection\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>webreflection</span></a></span> maybe a little hard to explain on text but given an arbitrary deeply nested object, I want to add metadata to each property that stores an arbitrary string for that property. the approach I’m using is to convert (for boolean types) primitive booleans to object booleans to add that data and retain the same behavior</p>",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1947351,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@vrugtehagel/115374568541104031",
			"author": {
				"name": "vrugtehagel",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@vrugtehagel",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/e6050d72eeee436de617b443c8cb08a5efd190d4c2cbfa610eaead9cb69cccef.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-14T21:10:04.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> it's not possible - see <a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@vrugtehagel/115308994476955114\"><span>https://</span><span>mastodon.social/@vrugtehagel/1</span><span>15308994476955114</span></a></p><p>If you want to have metadata for properties, you're probably best off wrapping them with a proxy and using a mechanism (like a prefix or named symbols) to look up the metadata without those properties being included in `Object.keys()` and whatnot.</p>",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
